        "interim housing"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "No NOFA; the Behavioral Health Bureau programs capital and subsidies through contracts. The June 2026 Board item also reported 22 prevention providers losing MHSA PEI funding under the BHSA restructuring.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "Monterey County's Housing and Community Development Department (HCD, Craig Spencer, Director; Darby Marshall, Housing Program Manager) runs the Inclusionary Housing Ordinance, the Monterey County Housing Trust Fund, PLHA, the Urban County CDBG and HOME programs and County land dispositions; the County Administrative Office Homelessness Strategies and Initiatives Division (CAO-HSI) runs HHAP and the SHARE Center; the Health Department Behavioral Health Bureau holds BHSA; the Coalition of Homeless Services Providers leads the CoC (CA-506, shared with San Benito); and the Housing Authority of the County of Monterey (HACM) and its Development Corporation supply vouchers and develop housing. Salinas, Monterey, Seaside and other entitlement cities run their own programs (Pass 3). countyofmonterey.gov blocks automated access (pages and documents), so records were built from the Legistar web API client 'monterey' and its Granicus attachments, hamonterey.org, chsp.org, zoneomics and HCD tables. Monterey is budgeting roughly $1.1 million a year of BHSA capital, enough for a small PSH gap or acquisition contribution, plus about $900,000 a year of permanent rental subsidies that can be project-based; pair with HHAP-6 operating money and HACM vouchers. Source is the June 2026 Integrated Plan approval item (Legistar file 26-552) with the budget attachment.",
      "source_url": "https://monterey.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=65759&GUID=00E0137A-EBD5-4BAA-90FD-AB36F812A89A",
